{"duration_api_ms":462245,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"ced00b5d-e3f4-4308-be9f-3266f08d99c9","total_cost_usd":1.9518754000000007,"usage":{"input_tokens":172,"cache_creation_input_tokens":86858,"cache_read_input_tokens":6211587,"output_tokens":35761,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":6896},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":86858,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2664,"cache_read_input_tokens":102657,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1225,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1225},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":4072,"outputTokens":20,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.004172,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":172,"outputTokens":35761,"cacheReadInputTokens":6211587,"cacheCreationInputTokens":86858,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.9477034000000006,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":6896,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":106,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":\"Deployed a 3-node RabbitMQ cluster (node1/node2/node3, RHEL 9) with AMQP over mutual TLS using a self-generated cluster CA, and a management interface restricted to the cluster subnet. Verified functional TLS client-cert enforcement, cluster health, and completed the mandatory sequential restart-and-recovery protocol on all three nodes with boot-identity proof.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Installed Erlang 26 and RabbitMQ 3.13.7 on node1, node2, node3 via rabbitmq/erlang and rabbitmq/rabbitmq-server packagecloud repos\",\"Populated /etc/hosts with CLUSTER_HOSTS and set an identical Erlang cookie (via secret_env) on all three nodes for clustering\",\"Generated a dedicated cluster CA on node1 (RSA 4096, 10yr) plus per-node server certs (SANs for node name/localhost/own IP) and a client cert for mTLS; also generated an untrusted CA + client cert for negative testing\",\"Distributed CA cert and per-node server cert/key to node2 and node3 over SSH using the cluster keypair\",\"Configured /etc/rabbitmq/rabbitmq.conf on each node: disabled plaintext AMQP (listeners.tcp = none), enabled AMQPS on 5671 with verify_peer and fail_if_no_peer_cert=true, bound management listener to the node's own cluster IP, configured classic_config peer discovery\",\"Enabled rabbitmq_management plugin and started rabbitmq-server on all nodes; confirmed automatic cluster formation\",\"Added firewalld rules on all three nodes: opened 5671/tcp broadly for AMQPS clients, restricted 15672 (management), 25672 (clustering), and 4369 (epmd) to source 10.100.162.0/24 only\",\"Created a test RabbitMQ user and ran real AMQP-over-TLS publish/consume via Python+pika using the CA-issued client cert (success), and using the untrusted-CA client cert (rejected with TLS unknown_ca alert), including a cross-node test from node2 to node1\",\"Verified server-side enforcement via RabbitMQ logs showing 'certificate_required' alert with no client cert and 'Unknown CA' alert with the untrusted cert\",\"Created a durable, HA-mirrored queue with a persistent message on node1 as a data-durability probe\",\"Captured boot_id baseline on all three nodes, then sequentially rebooted node1, waited for recovery and full cluster health, then node2, then node3, verifying changed boot_id and full 3-node cluster/listener recovery after each restart\",\"Re-verified post-restart: durable message still present, valid mTLS client still works end-to-end, untrusted-CA client still rejected\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"RabbitMQ cluster running across node1/node2/node3\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-8bfd605e815e4c43\",\"cmd-9c40cb3f713e40b6\",\"cmd-7cd67c802e6a4f52\",\"cmd-ce30a8c8df4f4c95\"],\"summary\":\"rabbitmqctl cluster_status shows all three nodes as running disk nodes both before and after the restart sequence\"},{\"requirement\":\"Custom CA created for the cluster and used to issue node/client certs\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-50be5a3037654d17\",\"cmd-5fecaa83bf2d4b81\",\"cmd-a9cc74cb27c3410a\"],\"summary\":\"openssl generated a self-signed CA, per-node server certs signed by it, and a client cert signed by it plus a separate untrusted CA for negative testing\"},{\"requirement\":\"AMQP over TLS enforced, only clients with certs from this CA accepted\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-d173202a0a8241fa\",\"cmd-b0ac0e54a6ad4d1c\",\"cmd-4add14a8bfc14fab\",\"cmd-828df7ff54cb48d6\",\"cmd-3f3bf82ae5da4a29\",\"cmd-2b7b88d8e6cd4a23\"],\"summary\":\"RabbitMQ log shows fatal TLS alerts (certificate_required, Unknown CA) rejecting missing/foreign-CA client certs; pika client with CA-issued cert completes a full publish/consume over AMQPS from both node1 and node2, while the untrusted-CA client is rejected with an SSL unknown_ca error\"},{\"requirement\":\"Management interface reachable only from within the cluster\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-812eaaa97c154093\",\"cmd-6c8f97d76c1d474d\",\"cmd-980fc9f626fb402c\",\"cmd-aa341db2f6104222\",\"cmd-badffe9de04e46e4\",\"cmd-18ad712ddcea4d8d\"],\"summary\":\"firewalld/nft rules on all three nodes only accept port 15672 from source 10.100.162.0/24 (all other sources fall through to default deny); confirmed reachable from node2 to node1's management API over the cluster network\"},{\"requirement\":\"Healthy baseline captured before restarts\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-f30b59ca19ea4db4\",\"cmd-42354b6a39d7446f\",\"cmd-d91b9ff24bd94de0\",\"cmd-f662a90edd4c491b\",\"cmd-511da696ffbd4cf8\",\"cmd-1ee7cafab0dc428b\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id on all three nodes and created/verified a durable, HA-mirrored queue with a persistent message prior to any restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart: ack, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-8f53ecd945154d62\",\"cmd-1bb97532c8d04997\",\"cmd-9c40cb3f713e40b6\",\"cmd-9c8a0eab51b84224\"],\"summary\":\"Reboot acknowledged (stream closed), boot_id changed from 67c52137... to 3d43725e..., cluster_status shows all 3 nodes running again, queue message and TLS/management listeners confirmed present after restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 restart: ack, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-809320cd47a1464b\",\"cmd-c6d09c49dd354cdc\",\"cmd-973fa1de4d9c43cc\",\"cmd-7cd67c802e6a4f52\"],\"summary\":\"Reboot acknowledged, boot_id changed from 555221a1... to 785331da..., cluster_status shows all 3 nodes running, AMQPS/management listeners back up\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 restart: ack, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-df99505b08af4e6f\",\"cmd-48b6b41a68a44f5f\",\"cmd-9904bfe3d6134b53\",\"cmd-ce30a8c8df4f4c95\"],\"summary\":\"Reboot acknowledged, boot_id changed from 34027437... to 35b6d70e..., cluster_status shows all 3 nodes running, AMQPS/management listeners back up\"},{\"requirement\":\"Final end-to-end verification after all restarts\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-0509b98f86f64b2a\"],\"summary\":\"Post-restart check confirms durable message still present (messages:1, state:running), CA-issued client still completes publish/consume, and untrusted-CA client is still rejected\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Deployed a 3-node RabbitMQ cluster (node1/node2/node3, RHEL 9) with AMQP over mutual TLS using a self-generated cluster CA, and a management interface restricted to the cluster subnet. Verified functional TLS client-cert enforcement, cluster health, and completed the mandatory sequential restart-and-recovery protocol on all three nodes with boot-identity proof.","actions_performed":["Installed Erlang 26 and RabbitMQ 3.13.7 on node1, node2, node3 via rabbitmq/erlang and rabbitmq/rabbitmq-server packagecloud repos","Populated /etc/hosts with CLUSTER_HOSTS and set an identical Erlang cookie (via secret_env) on all three nodes for clustering","Generated a dedicated cluster CA on node1 (RSA 4096, 10yr) plus per-node server certs (SANs for node name/localhost/own IP) and a client cert for mTLS; also generated an untrusted CA + client cert for negative testing","Distributed CA cert and per-node server cert/key to node2 and node3 over SSH using the cluster keypair","Configured /etc/rabbitmq/rabbitmq.conf on each node: disabled plaintext AMQP (listeners.tcp = none), enabled AMQPS on 5671 with verify_peer and fail_if_no_peer_cert=true, bound management listener to the node's own cluster IP, configured classic_config peer discovery","Enabled rabbitmq_management plugin and started rabbitmq-server on all nodes; confirmed automatic cluster formation","Added firewalld rules on all three nodes: opened 5671/tcp broadly for AMQPS clients, restricted 15672 (management), 25672 (clustering), and 4369 (epmd) to source 10.100.162.0/24 only","Created a test RabbitMQ user and ran real AMQP-over-TLS publish/consume via Python+pika using the CA-issued client cert (success), and using the untrusted-CA client cert (rejected with TLS unknown_ca alert), including a cross-node test from node2 to node1","Verified server-side enforcement via RabbitMQ logs showing 'certificate_required' alert with no client cert and 'Unknown CA' alert with the untrusted cert","Created a durable, HA-mirrored queue with a persistent message on node1 as a data-durability probe","Captured boot_id baseline on all three nodes, then sequentially rebooted node1, waited for recovery and full cluster health, then node2, then node3, verifying changed boot_id and full 3-node cluster/listener recovery after each restart","Re-verified post-restart: durable message still present, valid mTLS client still works end-to-end, untrusted-CA client still rejected"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"RabbitMQ cluster running across node1/node2/node3","command_ids":["cmd-8bfd605e815e4c43","cmd-9c40cb3f713e40b6","cmd-7cd67c802e6a4f52","cmd-ce30a8c8df4f4c95"],"summary":"rabbitmqctl cluster_status shows all three nodes as running disk nodes both before and after the restart sequence"},{"requirement":"Custom CA created for the cluster and used to issue node/client certs","command_ids":["cmd-50be5a3037654d17","cmd-5fecaa83bf2d4b81","cmd-a9cc74cb27c3410a"],"summary":"openssl generated a self-signed CA, per-node server certs signed by it, and a client cert signed by it plus a separate untrusted CA for negative testing"},{"requirement":"AMQP over TLS enforced, only clients with certs from this CA accepted","command_ids":["cmd-d173202a0a8241fa","cmd-b0ac0e54a6ad4d1c","cmd-4add14a8bfc14fab","cmd-828df7ff54cb48d6","cmd-3f3bf82ae5da4a29","cmd-2b7b88d8e6cd4a23"],"summary":"RabbitMQ log shows fatal TLS alerts (certificate_required, Unknown CA) rejecting missing/foreign-CA client certs; pika client with CA-issued cert completes a full publish/consume over AMQPS from both node1 and node2, while the untrusted-CA client is rejected with an SSL unknown_ca error"},{"requirement":"Management interface reachable only from within the cluster","command_ids":["cmd-812eaaa97c154093","cmd-6c8f97d76c1d474d","cmd-980fc9f626fb402c","cmd-aa341db2f6104222","cmd-badffe9de04e46e4","cmd-18ad712ddcea4d8d"],"summary":"firewalld/nft rules on all three nodes only accept port 15672 from source 10.100.162.0/24 (all other sources fall through to default deny); confirmed reachable from node2 to node1's management API over the cluster network"},{"requirement":"Healthy baseline captured before restarts","command_ids":["cmd-f30b59ca19ea4db4","cmd-42354b6a39d7446f","cmd-d91b9ff24bd94de0","cmd-f662a90edd4c491b","cmd-511da696ffbd4cf8","cmd-1ee7cafab0dc428b"],"summary":"Captured boot_id on all three nodes and created/verified a durable, HA-mirrored queue with a persistent message prior to any restart"},{"requirement":"node1 restart: ack, changed boot identity, recovered state","command_ids":["cmd-8f53ecd945154d62","cmd-1bb97532c8d04997","cmd-9c40cb3f713e40b6","cmd-9c8a0eab51b84224"],"summary":"Reboot acknowledged (stream closed), boot_id changed from 67c52137... to 3d43725e..., cluster_status shows all 3 nodes running again, queue message and TLS/management listeners confirmed present after restart"},{"requirement":"node2 restart: ack, changed boot identity, recovered state","command_ids":["cmd-809320cd47a1464b","cmd-c6d09c49dd354cdc","cmd-973fa1de4d9c43cc","cmd-7cd67c802e6a4f52"],"summary":"Reboot acknowledged, boot_id changed from 555221a1... to 785331da..., cluster_status shows all 3 nodes running, AMQPS/management listeners back up"},{"requirement":"node3 restart: ack, changed boot identity, recovered state","command_ids":["cmd-df99505b08af4e6f","cmd-48b6b41a68a44f5f","cmd-9904bfe3d6134b53","cmd-ce30a8c8df4f4c95"],"summary":"Reboot acknowledged, boot_id changed from 34027437... to 35b6d70e..., cluster_status shows all 3 nodes running, AMQPS/management listeners back up"},{"requirement":"Final end-to-end verification after all restarts","command_ids":["cmd-0509b98f86f64b2a"],"summary":"Post-restart check confirms durable message still present (messages:1, state:running), CA-issued client still completes publish/consume, and untrusted-CA client is still rejected"}]},"ttft_ms":4223,"type":"result","duration_ms":738789,"uuid":"1547d3c1-85c2-434c-9c45-959520b30efd","ttft_strea